menu "PaperColor experimental display pipeline"

config PAPERCOLOR_EXPERIMENTAL_LUT
    bool "Enable the experimental calibrated 5-bit color LUT"
    default n
    help
        Route Canvas refreshes through the generated 32 KiB CIEDE2000 LUT.
        This is disabled by default so production rendering remains unchanged.
        The bundled nominal profile is for pipeline validation only; regenerate
        the LUT from measured panel patches before evaluating physical color.

config PAPERCOLOR_NATIVE_CHART_ON_BOOT
    bool "Show native-pigment diagnostic chart at startup"
    default n
    help
        Calibration-only build: show six unmixed pigments and known-coverage
        mixtures without the photo algorithm. A returns to the normal home UI.
        Does not change stored photos/settings or the normal photo renderer.

config PAPERCOLOR_PRIMARY_WHITE_BUDGET
    bool "Limit extra white in single-pigment photo sectors (A/B candidate)"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_EXPERIMENTAL_LUT
    default n
    help
        For black/white plus one chromatic pigment only, preserve the target's
        neutral-white budget. Keep two-pigment hues and neutral targets on the
        accepted mapping. This is a rendering-policy experiment, not calibration.

config PAPERCOLOR_PRIMARY_PEAK_PRESERVATION
    bool "Preserve a full-scale primary peak with continuous hue falloff"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_PRIMARY_WHITE_BUDGET
    default n
    help
        Controlled chart candidate: prevent nearest-RGB projection from adding
        black merely to reduce a full-scale pigment's secondary RGB components.
        The nominal palette's blue reaches 255. Fade its correction continuously
        with source dominance across candidate masks; preserve neutral targets
        and equal-channel secondary hues. Leave red/green peak policies intact.
        This is a target policy, not a measured physical panel profile.

config PAPERCOLOR_BLUE_SECONDARY_BALANCE
    bool "Rebalance blue secondary hues while retaining neutral coverage"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_PRIMARY_PEAK_PRESERVATION
    default n
    help
        Controlled chart candidate for red/blue and green/blue mixtures. Move
        chromatic coverage toward source chroma ratios, retaining projected
        black and white amounts. Fade at low chroma and pigment boundaries.
        This is a hue policy experiment, not a measured physical color profile.

config PAPERCOLOR_SECONDARY_WHITE_REDUCTION
    bool "Gently reduce white in saturated blue secondary mixtures"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_BLUE_SECONDARY_BALANCE
    default n
    help
        Separate white-axis chart experiment: move at most one quarter of white
        coverage into the existing chromatic mixture. Preserve its pigment ratio
        and black target, with smooth fades at neutral and pigment boundaries.
        This can darken colors; physical chart acceptance is required.

config PAPERCOLOR_WARM_COMPENSATION_BYPASS
    bool "Bypass legacy thresholded warm-sector source compression"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_PRIMARY_WHITE_BUDGET
    default n
    help
        Controlled experiment: skip only the red-yellow source compression
        triggered at blue >= 32 and red-green >= 80. Keep target projection,
        white reduction, blue hue policies and diffusion unchanged. This
        removes those compensation switches but can increase white coverage
        in orange; physical full-chart acceptance is required.

config PAPERCOLOR_PURPLE_COMPENSATION_BYPASS
    bool "Bypass legacy thresholded red boost in blue-purple sources"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_PRIMARY_WHITE_BUDGET
    default n
    help
        Controlled single-branch experiment: skip the red-blue compensation
        enabled at B > R and 2R >= B. Keep green-blue compression, warm policy,
        projection, hue balance, white reduction and diffusion unchanged.
        Removes this switch but may darken purples and reduce red coverage;
        full-chart physical acceptance is required.

config PAPERCOLOR_PURPLE_COMPENSATION_SMOOTH
    bool "Smooth the legacy purple compensation activation ratio"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_PRIMARY_WHITE_BUDGET && !PAPERCOLOR_PURPLE_COMPENSATION_BYPASS
    default n
    help
        Replace the hard R/B=1/2 activation with a smoothstep across 2/5..5/8.
        Preserve no gain below the interval and the original integer gain
        above it. Other source sectors and downstream policies stay fixed.
        Experimental transition width, not measured physical calibration.

config PAPERCOLOR_CYAN_RATIO_SMOOTH
    bool "Smooth green-to-blue coverage transfer near cyan"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_PRIMARY_WHITE_BUDGET && PAPERCOLOR_BLUE_SECONDARY_BALANCE && PAPERCOLOR_SECONDARY_WHITE_REDUCTION
    default n
    help
        Experimental IMG_9955 cyan B direction: transfer up to 1/16 of
        chromatic coverage from green to blue, preserving white and black.
        Fade smoothly with source hue, chroma and pigment availability.
        Magenta and original blue-cyan edge targets remain unchanged.
        Requires gradient and full-chart physical acceptance.

config PAPERCOLOR_NATIVE_565_RECONSTRUCTION
    bool "Reconstruct native pigments in their RGB565 quantization cells"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_EXACT_PIGMENT_ANCHOR
    default n
    help
        Use the native RGB888 pigment as the representative of its exact
        RGB565 cell before photo processing. Removes quantization-only dots
        from native solids. Neighboring cells, RGB888 and UI nearest paths
        remain unchanged. Source colors sharing a cell are indistinguishable;
        this does not reconstruct arbitrary original RGB888 values.

config PAPERCOLOR_EXACT_PIGMENT_ANCHOR
    bool "Protect exact pigment targets from incoming diffusion residuals"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_PRIMARY_WHITE_BUDGET
    default n
    help
        Chart candidate: when the Q4 target exactly equals an allowed chromatic
        pigment, emit that pigment and absorb this pixel's incoming residual.
        This prevents boundary dots in representable solids. Do not snap near
        colors or alter neutral targets; mixtures still use normal diffusion.

config PAPERCOLOR_CHROMATIC_EDGE_GUARD
    bool "Keep exact two-pigment targets free of foreign boundary dots"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_EXACT_PIGMENT_ANCHOR
    default n
    help
        For targets on a red-blue or green-blue pigment segment, intercept
        attempted foreign dots, retain tangential error and choose between
        those two pigments. Preserve compatible choices and their residuals.
        Detect the segment before Q4 rounding; leave real black/white mixtures
        and all other targets unchanged. This does not alter the target mapping
        or diffusion weights. Full-chart and gradient validation is required.

config PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_PHOTO_ON_BOOT
    bool "Show embedded portrait reference at startup"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_PRIMARY_WHITE_BUDGET && !PAPERCOLOR_NATIVE_CHART_ON_BOOT
    default n
    help
        Test-only build: display Kodak image 04 with the current PhotoBalanced
        pipeline at startup. A returns home. Does not write photos or settings.

config PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_CHART_ON_BOOT
    bool "Show embedded source color chart at startup"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_PRIMARY_WHITE_BUDGET && !PAPERCOLOR_NATIVE_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_PHOTO_ON_BOOT
    default n
    help
        Test-only build: display the canonical 400x600 source color chart with
        PhotoBalanced at startup. Unlike the native-pigment diagnostic, this
        exercises the photo mapping and dither. A returns home. No storage writes.

config PAPERCOLOR_MIX_RATIO_CHART_ON_BOOT
    bool "Show controlled red/blue and green/blue mixture grids at startup"
    depends on !PAPERCOLOR_NATIVE_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_PHOTO_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_CHART_ON_BOOT
    default n
    help
        Diagnostic-only chart with independent white and chromatic fractions,
        emitted as exact native codes. A returns home. Does not alter the photo
        algorithm or stored photos/settings. Keep the same pattern in all cells.

config PAPERCOLOR_WHITE_AB_CHART_ON_BOOT
    bool "Show same-screen PhotoBalanced white reduction A/B at startup"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_SECONDARY_WHITE_REDUCTION && PAPERCOLOR_CHROMATIC_EDGE_GUARD
    depends on !PAPERCOLOR_NATIVE_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_PHOTO_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_MIX_RATIO_CHART_ON_BOOT
    default n
    help
        Display pre-rendered native crops from the actual source-chart photo
        pipeline with white reduction off/on. Hue policy and edge protection
        are identical. Duplicate A/B/B/A columns reveal uneven illumination.
        Does not change the normal photo renderer or stored photos/settings.

config PAPERCOLOR_WARM_AB_CHART_ON_BOOT
    bool "Show same-screen PhotoBalanced warm compensation A/B at startup"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_WARM_COMPENSATION_BYPASS && PAPERCOLOR_SECONDARY_WHITE_REDUCTION && PAPERCOLOR_CHROMATIC_EDGE_GUARD
    depends on !PAPERCOLOR_NATIVE_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_PHOTO_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_MIX_RATIO_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_WHITE_AB_CHART_ON_BOOT
    default n
    help
        Display pre-rendered full-source-chart crops with old warm compensation
        versus bypass. White reduction, hue policy and edge protection stay fixed.
        Duplicate A/B/B/A columns reveal uneven illumination. A returns home.
        Does not change the photo renderer or stored photos/settings.

config PAPERCOLOR_PURPLE_SMOOTH_AB_CHART_ON_BOOT
    bool "Show same-screen purple compensation transition A/B at startup"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_PURPLE_COMPENSATION_SMOOTH && PAPERCOLOR_WARM_COMPENSATION_BYPASS && PAPERCOLOR_SECONDARY_WHITE_REDUCTION && PAPERCOLOR_CHROMATIC_EDGE_GUARD
    depends on !PAPERCOLOR_NATIVE_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_PHOTO_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_MIX_RATIO_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_WHITE_AB_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_WARM_AB_CHART_ON_BOOT
    default n
    help
        Diagnostic native crops from complete PhotoBalanced renders. A retains
        the hard purple activation and B smooths it. Two new stimulus ramps
        exercise the transition; four canonical controls retain their output.
        Duplicate A/B/B/A columns reveal uneven illumination. A returns home.

config PAPERCOLOR_SECONDARY_RATIO_ABC_CHART_ON_BOOT
    bool "Show fixed-white secondary hue-ratio diagnostic at startup"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_PURPLE_COMPENSATION_SMOOTH && PAPERCOLOR_WARM_COMPENSATION_BYPASS && PAPERCOLOR_SECONDARY_WHITE_REDUCTION && PAPERCOLOR_CHROMATIC_EDGE_GUARD
    depends on !PAPERCOLOR_NATIVE_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_PHOTO_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_MIX_RATIO_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_WHITE_AB_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_WARM_AB_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_PURPLE_SMOOTH_AB_CHART_ON_BOOT
    default n
    help
        Pre-rendered PhotoBalanced diagnostic crops: current ratio and +/-6.25
        percentage points of colored red/green coverage, white target fixed.
        The host-only probe changes only the two diagnostic sources. Normal
        photo mapping and the accepted home renderer remain unchanged.

config PAPERCOLOR_CYAN_RATIO_AB_CHART_ON_BOOT
    bool "Show same-screen smooth cyan ratio A/B at startup"
    depends on PAPERCOLOR_CYAN_RATIO_SMOOTH && PAPERCOLOR_PURPLE_COMPENSATION_SMOOTH && PAPERCOLOR_WARM_COMPENSATION_BYPASS && PAPERCOLOR_CHROMATIC_EDGE_GUARD
    depends on !PAPERCOLOR_NATIVE_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_PHOTO_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_REFERENCE_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_MIX_RATIO_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_WHITE_AB_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_WARM_AB_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_PURPLE_SMOOTH_AB_CHART_ON_BOOT && !PAPERCOLOR_SECONDARY_RATIO_ABC_CHART_ON_BOOT
    default n
    help
        Actual PhotoBalanced A/B crops: current baseline versus smoothly
        reduced green coverage near cyan. Includes source cyan, two ramps,
        magenta/light-purple/blue-cyan controls and native anchors.
        A/B/B/A repeats show lighting variation. Button A returns home.

endmenu
